            {
                "entry_id": "9231b134-2ccc-30d0-bd46-5ee1780394c4",
                "word": "vulnéraire",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "29fc5302-22e5-47be-8c35-c40ccc44d0ad",
                        "entry_id": "9231b134-2ccc-30d0-bd46-5ee1780394c4",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "vulnéraires"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "225db995-a44c-31ae-bbfa-9cc028db6bac",
                        "entry_id": "9231b134-2ccc-30d0-bd46-5ee1780394c4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui guérit les plaies."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d0e0563-d4ca-44ca-a1da-53fe5bdf1fd9",
                                "sense_id": "225db995-a44c-31ae-bbfa-9cc028db6bac",
                                "text": "La sanicle est une de ces plantes autrefois célèbres, comme vulnéraires ; […]. Elle est utile pour déterger les ulcères."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "632bf603-16ce-455d-87e3-24965325894e",
                                "sense_id": "225db995-a44c-31ae-bbfa-9cc028db6bac",
                                "text": "Au sortir du cimetière, plusieurs assistantes voulaient faire prendre quelque chose à Marie, chez le marchand de vins, pour la remettre : un kirsch ou un vulnéraire, les deux au besoin, il paraît que c’est très bon pour les enfants."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d8431f58-224a-4d82-843a-aa4950866ea3",
                                "sense_id": "225db995-a44c-31ae-bbfa-9cc028db6bac",
                                "text": "– Et le vulnéraire opère bien : nous avons imbibé le pansement de teinture d’aloès. Faute d’aristoloche."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6d5e5022-0449-41a5-bd4b-0d3ae8681b01",
                                "sense_id": "225db995-a44c-31ae-bbfa-9cc028db6bac",
                                "text": "Ce n'est pas lui qui m'a versé un verre de vulnéraire, ou d'arquebuse, après ma chute sur la tête dans la fosse du garage."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e3558d5e-ed05-4337-91db-4aa31e775a98",
                        "source_entry_id": "9231b134-2ccc-30d0-bd46-5ee1780394c4",
                        "source_sense_id": "225db995-a44c-31ae-bbfa-9cc028db6bac",
                        "target_lang_word": "vulnerary",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "vulnerary",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c9dc4e42-df4b-3e22-aa33-e7f2a52e8bfd",
                                        "entry_id": "36bb0d22-fb01-35a8-a5a8-a5c6b691ec54",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Useful or used for healing wounds; curative, healing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02f51238-d4cc-4ddb-8597-5b48eba0abad",
                                                "sense_id": "c9dc4e42-df4b-3e22-aa33-e7f2a52e8bfd",
                                                "text": "Rebecca examined the wound, and having applied to it such vulnerary remedies as her art prescribed, informed her father that […] there was nothing to fear for his guest’s life."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d6c56d0-f64a-484e-a79c-d1539ac2dfc1",
                                                "sense_id": "c9dc4e42-df4b-3e22-aa33-e7f2a52e8bfd",
                                                "text": "Take, for example, the famous vulnerary ointment attributed to Paracelsus."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3dfd5fa2-90a0-30d7-a503-07aff3b0fad3",
                                        "entry_id": "36bb0d22-fb01-35a8-a5a8-a5c6b691ec54",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Causing wounds; wounding."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "vulnerary",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d33214c9-3447-30e1-b437-433e6f3de1bb",
                                        "entry_id": "d1838d2e-1f0f-3d11-99eb-7c8753a1b4f6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A healing drug or other agent used in healing and treating wounds."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a9e5d07-c96c-43af-b68a-5be084f322d7",
                                                "sense_id": "d33214c9-3447-30e1-b437-433e6f3de1bb",
                                                "text": "On the ſurface of the water there floats a liquid bitumen, although it be every day ſcummed off, as it doth on the lake Aſphaltites in Judæa: The Inhabitants uſe it as pitch: it is alſo found to be an excellent vulnerary, and good in curing old cacoethic and ſcrophulous ulcers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "381fbbfa-625d-45ed-bb45-48ecc75f5012",
                        "source_entry_id": "9231b134-2ccc-30d0-bd46-5ee1780394c4",
